{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Do not fear.</b> Meaning, that He would speak with you still more, <b>for in order</b> etc. And HaShem had already carried out His good design and made them a sign, for they were singled out for good, for their zohamah (impurity) ceased through the intermediary of the word of Elohim. And also a second reason: <b>in order that</b> etc. — meaning, for through the uprooting of the zohamah from them, they acquired the fear, which is His Shechinah, blessed be He, a place to be continually upon their faces, for the image of Elohim with which HaShem created man in His image returned to its original state. And the upshot of these two things is ״לְבִלְתִּי תֶחֱטָאוּ״ (לא תחטא), for whoever possesses shame of face, which is the fear aforementioned, does not readily sin." "It further intends in His saying <b>in order to test you</b>, so that you should have no complaint why HaShem does not make all Israel prophesy — behold, He tested them with prophecy and they could not endure."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:31:13.314614742Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}